  "narrative": "The newly delivered panel gives no support for accepting any clinically meaningful stronger-dependency association. All estimates are already signed toward the registered stronger-dependency direction, so positive values favor the claims and negative values oppose them. The feature_048 level_001 versus level_003 panel is internally inconsistent: H33, H34, and H38 are near null or opposite with upper bounds below the approximate 10% outcome-specific thresholds, H37 is only a small positive estimate below the threshold, H39 is statistically opposed rather than supportive, and the H40 interaction with feature_034 is opposite/null with a wide interval. These results do not corroborate the earlier borderline H16 result, so H16 and the related feature_048 follow-ups are closed as unsupported. The feature_030 cross-outcome panel is also inconsistent: H35, H36, H41, and H42 are near null or opposite, with point estimates far below clinically meaningful positive magnitudes, despite wide intervals in some cases admitting small effects. This provides no corroboration for the earlier H24 borderline positive result, so H24 and its follow-ups are closed. H25 and H44 are also null and closed. As a critical reviewer, the main competing explanations for the few near-boundary positive estimates are chance under repeated unadjusted discovery testing, wide uncertainty, and outcome-specific noise; there is no leakage evident in the Welch independent-cell diagnostics, and cell-count requirements are satisfied except that some small categorical cells remain imprecise. The opposite-sign H39 result is noted but is inconsistent with other feature_048 outcomes and does not justify a new reversed claim. No validation is requested because validating a single marginal candidate is premature; the remaining priority is direct cross-outcome testing of the stronger feature_028 signal already registered in H47-H51. These are associations in this supplied dataset only, not causal or generalizable findings.",
  "research_notes": "Interim accepted set: empty. Validation delivered: none. Current conclusions: feature_048 and feature_030 candidate predictors are now closed because lower-threshold cross-outcome tests are null, inconsistent, or opposite despite earlier borderline single-outcome results. H25 and H44 are null and closed. Remaining priority signal: H43 reversed feature_028 level_003 versus level_002 on outcome_011, signed +0.0427 versus approximate threshold ~0.030, but its 95% interval is -0.0042 to 0.0895 and comparator cell n=98, so it remains unresolved and active. Next analysis priority: run H47-H51 direct feature_028 level_003 versus level_002 on outcome_002/012/015/003/005. Approximate 10% absolute thresholds using overall outcome means: outcome_002 ~0.026, outcome_003/005/012/015 ~0.025, outcome_011 ~0.030. Acceptance requires either one validation result with lower bound above zero and clinically meaningful magnitude or multiple direct feature_028 outcomes with positive point estimates near/above thresholds and reasonably nonoverlapping null intervals. If H47-H51 are also null or inconsistent, close feature_028 and stop broad categorical screening; shift to a small number of numeric quantile/interaction contrasts or accept the dataset-level negative conclusion. Maintain multiplicity caution: all tests are unadjusted discovery tests; no causal interpretation."
